  "chapter": {
    "number": 37,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(38) A Psalm of David for remembrance concerning the Sabbath-day."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, rebuke me not in your wrath, neither chasten me in your anger.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For your weapons are fixed in me, and you have pressed your hand heavily upon me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For there is no health in my flesh because of your anger; there is no peace to my bones because of my sins.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For my transgressions have gone over my head: they have pressed heavily upon me like a weighty burden.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My bruises have become noisome and corrupt, because of my foolishness.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I have been wretched and bowed down continually: I went with a mourning countenance all the day.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For my soul is filled with mockings; and there is no health in my flesh.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I have been afflicted and brought down exceedingly: I have roared for the groaning of my heart.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But all my desire is before you; and my groaning is not hidden from you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My heart is troubled, my strength has failed me; and the light of my eyes is not with me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My friends and my neighbors drew near before me, and stood still; and my nearest of kin stood afar off.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "While they pressed hard upon me that sought my soul: and they that sought my hurt spoke vanities, and devised deceits all the day.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But I, as a deaf man, heard not; and was as a dumb man not opening his mouth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And I was as a man that hears not, and who has no reproofs in his mouth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For I hoped in you, O Lord: you will hear, O Lord my God.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For I said, Lest my enemies rejoice against me: for when my feet were moved, they spoke boastingly against me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For I am ready for",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 72
          },
          {
            "text": "plagues, and my grief is continually before me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For I will declare my iniquity, and be distressed for my sin.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But my enemies live, and are mightier than I: and they that hate me unjustly are multiplied.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They that reward evil for good slandered me; because I followed righteousness.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Forsake me not, O Lord my God: depart not from me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Draw near to my help, O Lord of my salvation.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 72,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. scourges.",
